<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African negotiates air rights with China.</title>
<headline>S.African negotiates air rights with China.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa is negotiating with China to obtain overflying rights for flights to Japan because of the decision to break diplomatic ties with Taiwan, Deputy Foreign Minister Aziz Pahad said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Taiwan has suspended landing rights for (state-owned airline) SAA and overflying rights to Japan, and this means we also have to negotiate with the People's Republic of China to see whether prior to achieving diplomatic recognition, they will give us overflying rights to apan,&quot; Pahad told a parliamentary news briefing.</p>
<p>President Nelson Mandela said last year South Africa would scrap its diplomatic ties with Taiwan by the end of 1997 so that it could establish formal links with China.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +2721 403-2502</p>
